  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the minimum probability of any outcome in each lottery—i.e., the smallest single probability mass assigned. For A, it is 100%; for B, it is 1%. The reason would prefer A. However, the individual chooses B and justifies this by emphasizing the 99% chance of winning at least 2400, which is the complement of the 1% minimum probability outcome. The individual is not focusing on the minimum probability per se, but rather on the high probability of a favorable outcome. The reasoning is related to probability thresholds but does not align with the definition of the decision reason, which would favor A due to its higher minimum probability. The individual’s justification is based on maximizing upside with acceptable risk, not on maximizing the minimum probability of any single outcome. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
